// ─── Reports Registry ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Two centralised tables drive every report card on the site:
//
//   ReportUrls.reports.<image_ref>   ← the image URL (chart PNG)
//   REPORT_REGISTRY                  ← which page/slot each report appears in
//
// REPORT_REGISTRY entries carry the click-through library item id, the image
// reference (key into ReportUrls.reports), the alt text, plus placement fields
// consumed by the Python static-site generator (_build/build.py):
//
//   page     : "floor" | "tenant_floor" | "tenant_index" | "incomer" | "home"
//   floor    : floor key (used by page="floor" and page="tenant_floor")
//   tenant   : tenant slug (used by page="tenant_floor" and page="tenant_index")
//   incomer  : incomer key (used by page="incomer")
//   slot     : "electricity" | "heat" | "main" | "top" | "summary"
//                — section on the page
//   position : integer order within (page, …, slot)
//   title    : optional banner title (home + incomer_electricity headed cards)
//   kind     : optional render variant — "headed" for the report_card_headed macro
//
// Build behaviour: each builder filters REPORT_REGISTRY by the page's
// placement and uses the matching rows in position order. YAML may still
// supply an explicit `reports:` list to bypass the registry per page.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

